    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the change so that `POST /api/owners` rejects with **400** when the owner's email domain is on the disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n\nFollowing the repo's existing Bean Validation conventions (mirroring `TelephoneValidation`/`TelephoneValidator`), I:\n\n1. **`EmailDomainValidation.java`** \u2014 a new Bean Validation constraint annotation with a descriptive message.\n2. **`EmailDomainValidator.java`** \u2014 the `ConstraintValidator`. It treats absent/blank emails as valid (email is optional; syntax is handled by `format: email`), extracts the domain after the final `@`, and rejects case-insensitively against the fixed blocklist.\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `x-field-extra-annotation` on the `email` field so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` carries `@EmailDomainValidation`. Because controller args are already validated, a blocked domain now raises `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, which the existing `ExceptionControllerAdvice` maps to a `400 Bad Request` with the standard problem-detail body.\n\nThis wiring also covers the update path, since both create and update bind through the same validated DTO.",
